Thu Aug 20 08:50:40 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Convert the Python binding to the shared %treesitter_python_install
  loader: install upstream's pure-Python package files and generate
  a _binding.py that loads the grammar library this package ships.
  Drop %treesitter_python_build and the python devel/pip/wheel
  BuildRequires; the parser is no longer compiled a second time.
- Pin the python subpackage on the grammar package exactly
  (tree-sitter-verilog = version-release).
- Suggests python-tree-sitter >= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.
- Run a functional %check parsing Verilog through the shim; gated
  to suse_version >= 1699 because python-tree-sitter does not exist
  in Leap 16.0.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jul 27 08:36:32 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package of tree-sitter-verilog 1.0.3:
  * Verilog grammar library for the tree-sitter parsing
    framework (libtree-sitter-verilog.so grammar module)
  * Python binding built from the bundled bindings/python as
    pythonXYZ flavor subpackages via the shared
    %treesitter_python_build/_install macros
